or_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Claimed after certified plan-review PASS; beginning held-out TDD in worktree janitor-c195-03cd.","timestamp":1788482923412874602},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Starting held-out GREEN implementation in /Users/joeoakhart/janitor-c195-03cd. Scope: remove Python facade and MCP reconcile(mode=...) contract while preserving explicit bridge operations and CLI/engine routes.","timestamp":1788485160888102426},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Held-out GREEN implementation complete in /Users/joeoakhart/janitor-c195-03cd. Removed `rebar.reconcile` from the Python facade/API baseline and removed the MCP `reconcile` tool registration/classification/reference special cases. Kept explicit bridge operations intact and updated visible tests/docs/consumers to use/assert `bridge_preview`, `bridge_sync`, `bridge_run`, `bridge_fsck`, and `bridge_status`.\n\nValidation run from the janitor worktree:\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/interfaces/facades/test_library.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_programmatic.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_programmatic_heldout.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_manifest_compat_heldout.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_output_schema_coverage.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_surface.py tests/unit/test_api_surface_gate.py tests/unit/test_gen_mcp_reference.py tests/unit/test_mcp_library_parity.py -q` -> 177 passed.\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python scripts/gen_api_surface.py --check && env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py --check && env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m rebar.schemas.check_mcp_models --check` -> exit 0.\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint` -> exit 0 (ruff, format, complexity, mechanism, parity, and repo gates passed).\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck` -> Success: no issues found in 753 source files.\n- Smoke assertion: `rebar` has no `reconcile`, MCP tool list has no `reconcile`, and bridge_preview/sync/run/fsck/status remain registered -> passed.","timestamp":1788485804654229431}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788314439476447001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"412f8717-a40a-4e66-bd5e-f4c933367de9","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"3b66-615c-fbfb-4b1f"},{"link_uuid":"34bcc6ea-6e3d-4af7-a6ab-4deb50e8e7a9","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7217-4519-085c-4d13"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/_lib_ops.py` and `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py` retain Python-library and MCP `reconcile(mode=...)` compatibility adapters after explicit bridge operations were introduced. ADR 0092 accepted those adapters only as compatibility surfaces and reserved their removal until a separate deprecation decision after real consumers migrated. This ticket is that pre-1.0 deprecation/removal decision for the Python facade and MCP tool surfaces; the CLI `rebar reconcile` adapter is out of scope and remains available for CLI reconciliation flows, including `_bridge_runner.MODE_COMMANDS`.\n\nThe dependency `nosy-drooly-milksnake` delivered the canonical diagnostic/bridge contract and established the explicit replacement surfaces:\n\n- `dry-run` repository/Python/MCP compatibility consumers migrate to `bridge_preview`.\n- mutating sync/reconcile consumers migrate to `bridge_sync` or scheduled `bridge_run` as appropriate.\n- `reconcile-check` diagnostic observables migrate to `bridge_fsck` / `bridge_status`; they are not folded into `bridge_preview`.\n\n## Approach\n\nRemove the Python and MCP `reconcile(mode=...)` entrypoints and their published exports, examples, coverage exemptions, and generated/baseline surface artifacts. Replace repository consumers within this scope with explicit `bridge_preview`, `bridge_sync`, `bridge_run`, `bridge_fsck`, or `bridge_status` operations according to the mode semantics above. Preserve the canonical explicit bridge operations and their result/error contracts.\n\nKnown in-repository consumers/artifacts to update include `README.md`, `docs/release-notes.md`, `src/rebar/__init__.py`, library/facade/MCP tests, generated MCP reference tests, `api_surface_baseline.json`, `mcp_library_parity_manifest.json`, and the MCP output-schema coverage exemption for the legacy untyped reconcile tool. Do not remove the CLI `rebar reconcile` command or bridge-runner CLI dependency.\n\n## Scope\n\n- library/MCP operation definitions and exports\n- generated MCP models/references and surface baselines/exemptions for the removed MCP/Python adapters\n- docs/examples and changelog/release-note migration guidance\n- static, dynamic, string, and monkeypatch consumers within the declared Python/MCP scope\n\n## Testing\n\nAssert removed Python and MCP calls fail at signature/schema/tool-name validation before reconciliation work begins. Run explicit bridge operation result-contract tests for `bridge_preview`, `bridge_sync`, `bridge_run`, `bridge_fsck`, and `bridge_status` so canonical contracts remain stable.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Python and MCP `reconcile(mode=...)` contracts, examples, and exports are removed; the CLI `rebar reconcile` surface remains intact.\n- [x] Every repository consumer within the declared Python/MCP scope calls one explicit canonical bridge operation, including `bridge_fsck` / `bridge_status` for former reconcile-check diagnostics.\n- [x] Old library/MCP invocations fail at signature/schema/tool-name validation before work begins.\n- [x] Explicit bridge operations retain their documented result and error contracts.\n- [x] Surface baselines/exemptions and changelog/release-note documentation record the pre-1.0 Python/MCP `reconcile(mode=...)` removal and migration path.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_ops.py","reason":"remove rebar.reconcile(mode=...) compatibility entrypoint"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py","reason":"remove MCP reconcile(mode=...) compatibility tool/input"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_models.py","reason":"update generated result/input models if legacy contract owns them"},{"path":"src/rebar/__init__.py","reason":"remove public Python alias export"},{"path":"README.md","reason":"public rebar.reconcile(\"dry-run\") examples must be replaced with explicit bridge operations (AC: replace Python/MCP reconcile examples)"},{"path":"scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py","reason":"generator special-cases the reconcile MCP tool; remove/adjust that special-case when the MCP reconcile tool is removed"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/check_mcp_models.py","reason":"MCP-model drift checker owns the reconcile model declaration/exemption logic; update it when the reconcile MCP models are removed"},{"path":"docs","reason":"replace Python/MCP reconcile examples with explicit bridge operations"},{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","reason":"record pre-1.0 API/MCP breaking removal"},{"path":"tests","reason":"prove old calls reject and bridge operations preserve result contracts"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","3b66-615c-fbfb-4b1f"],["parent","0cfc-e511-8f8a-4c8b"],["relates_to","7217-4519-085c-4d13"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"0cfc-e511-8f8a-4c8b","parent_status_uuid":"87477075-7de3-48c2-bdcb-a634032114b9","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["janitor","reconciler","mcp","api","breaking-change"],"ticket_id":"c195-03cd-fc03-4ae0","ticket_type":"story","title":"Remove reconcile compatibility from Python and MCP contracts","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c5636ca4-7a7f-4f4c-947e-1f89757d43fc","c6c063b5-9f63-4d5c-8180-d6a1b15f0d6b","a1dee9e6-f106-46b9-9d53-767